Review the following PR.

## PR Information
- **Title**: Retry transient Windows filesystem errors via fileutil
- **Author**: testauthor
- **Branch**: feat/fileutil → main
- **Files Changed**: 1

## PR Description
Replace os.Remove with fileutil.Remove, which retries transient Windows filesystem errors and wraps the underlying error with fmt.Errorf.

## Diff

```diff
diff --git a/common/pkg/socket/socket.go b/common/pkg/socket/socket.go
index 1111111..2222222 100644
--- a/common/pkg/socket/socket.go
+++ b/common/pkg/socket/socket.go
@@ -50,10 +50,10 @@ func Listen(path string) (net.Listener, error) {
 	// Remove any stale socket file left over from a previous run before we
 	// bind. A missing file is fine — that is the normal startup case.
-	err := os.Remove(path)
+	err := fileutil.Remove(path)
 	if err != nil && !os.IsNotExist(err) {
 		return nil, fmt.Errorf("failed to remove socket: %w", err)
 	}
 	return net.Listen("unix", path)
 }
```
